    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>A dynasty from western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> that ruled northern India from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kannauj">Kannauj</a> between the early 9th and early 10th centuries.</li><li>Its cavalry checked Arab expansion beyond <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sindh">Sindh</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/multan">Multan</a>, and Arab writers thought its king the most hostile to them in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>.</li><li>It fought the Palas and Rashtrakutas for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kannauj">Kannauj</a>, and its feudatories became the later <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajputs">Rajput</a> kingdoms.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>An inscription of 876 at the Chaturbhuj temple in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gwalior-fort">Gwalior Fort</a>, set up under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mihira-bhoja">Mihira Bhoja</a>, contains one of the earliest known inscribed zeros in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>.</p></aside>
    </section>

